[0.0, "o", "# Mariano's collector 1.8.0rc4: walkthrough, PART 2 (recorded 2026-11-02 on Hamza's workstation, Windows 11, NOT\r\n"]
[0.359, "o", "# on the client's VM). Every command runs for real while it is recorded; nothing is typed in afterwards.\r\n"]
[0.703, "o", "#\r\n"]
[1.062, "o", "# Why there is a part 2: part 1 ended without warning at 13:45:43Z. The workstation ran short of memory (a web\r\n"]
[1.422, "o", "# browser opened for a sign-in) and the tool that ran the recording stopped its background tasks: the recorder,\r\n"]
[1.765, "o", "# and the collector with it, in the middle of Q2's resume (row 26 School Office, after its fourth page step). It\r\n"]
[2.125, "o", "# is a second, UNPLANNED forced stop of Q2 (the first, at 13:13:01Z, was the planned kill). Nothing else changed:\r\n"]
[2.469, "o", "# same release 1.8.0rc4, same database, same configuration, same limits (95 submissions per run; ceiling 200 /\r\n"]
[2.812, "o", "# USD 0.30). Q2 is resumed once more below; then its export and checks, which part 1 did not reach.\r\n"]
[3.172, "o", "#\r\n"]
